WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.720
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.230
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.010
Wow!
There’s so many vegetables!

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.710
Don’t they look tasty?

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.880
They’re fresh from the farm,
so they still have leaves and dirt on them.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.410
Huh...

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:33.890
The vegetables came with a letter from Endo,
a student of Sakuragi’s.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.890
He says that he took up farming
two years ago.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:44.640
Supposedly, Digda and Dugtrio suddenly turned up
in his fields recently, and they’re causing him trouble.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.220
Digda! Mole Pokémon!
Ground type!

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:56.030
It chews on plant roots underground!
It can cause damage to certain delicate vegetable crops!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.260
Dugtrio! Mole Pokémon!
Ground type!

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.080
The evolved form of Digda!
These triplets have super effective teamwork!

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.760
We can go scope out that!

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.300
I really want to catch
Digda and Dugtrio!

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.450
I thought you’d say that.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.550
Huh? Koharu?

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.800
Good morning!

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.590
I decided to have Koharu
help you out this time.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.140
Say hello to Endo for me.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.910
Sure! I’ll thank him for
the vegetables, too.

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.260
I’ll see you later, okay?

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.650
Go and investigate thoroughly,
and don’t forget to have lots of fun.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.950
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.550
It’s huge!

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.930
Eevee, look at this.
It’s a really nice view!

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.310
Yahoo!

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:09.190
Huh? Hey!
Why are you running?!

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.710
Wide, open spaces
just make you want to run!

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.280
Yeah!

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.170
What?!

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.460
Well, whatever.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:03.130
Here it is!

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.580
We’re here, we’re here.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.730
Eevee! Are you okay?

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.150
It’s a Biriridama!

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:22.760
Biriridama! Ball Pokémon!
Electric type!

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:27.240
Usually found in power plants!
It resembles a Monster Ball!

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:30.520
All right, I’m gonna catch you—

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:36.130
Hold on! Sorry... But that’s my precious partner
who helps me tend to the fields.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:38.750
Mr. Endo?!

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:43.380
Hi, Koharu.
Thank you for coming all this way.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.110
It’s been such a long time.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:52.890
You’ve really grown! When I was at Sakuragi’s lab,
you were still only this tall!

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.890
And you’re Satoshi
and Go, right?

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:02.990
Nice to meet you,
and welcome to Endo Farm.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.890
Nice to meet you.

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.240
A pleasure to meet you.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.470
Okay then,
let’s go put your bags inside.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:18.130
Before I show you the problem area,
try some of my prized fresh vegetables.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.760
Go on, pick whatever you’d like.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.270
All right!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:28.620
Huh, so this is how
tomatoes are grown.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.160
You never knew that?!

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.140
N-No, I knew it was a thing.
I’d just never seen it before...

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:38.940
Go ahead, take a big bite!

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.130
<i>Thanks for the food!</i>

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.890
It’s really tasty!

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:47.100
It’s more like a fruit
than a vegetable!

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.070
It’s sweet and smells great!

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:54.830
That makes me really happy!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.480
I took up farming
hoping to see smiles like yours.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.520
Both research and farming
give you the satisfaction of helping people out!

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.340
Go on, have some more!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.230
Thank you very much!

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:07.970
I’d never get tired of eating these!

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.470
This soil is great!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.170
Oh, you can tell?

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.930
Well, I look after the
flowers at school.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:21.730
What I do is I crush molted Gorogna shells
and use them as fertilizer!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:22.460
Huh?

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.280
Ack!

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.500
Thanks for the treat!

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:34.040
So, Mr. Endo.
Where are the Digda and Dugtrio?

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:37.040
This way. I’ll show you.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:45.310
This is the largest field
here at Endo Farm.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:47.630
Currently I’m growing carrots here.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.490
Oh, the Biriridama from earlier!

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.750
It’s pulling out weeds!

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:01.400
Yeah. And it’s much better at it than me.
It’s really dependable.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.400
You’re amazing!

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:06.650
Are you okay?

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.290
I’m used to this...

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:14.780
Could this be...

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.660
There! Digda!

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.790
No way!

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.710
Over there, and over here!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.020
There’s so many Digda!

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.710
You can see my issue.

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:40.430
For some reason, Digda suddenly started
showing up in my field not too long ago.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:44.810
Biriridama watches for them,
but can’t keep up with them...

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:51.700
With them running around, the carrots will get ruined.
What’s more, we’re on harvest season...

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:56.200
So being at my wits’ end,
I asked the Professor for help.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.310
For now, we need to do something
about the Digda.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.950
I’ll chase ‘em out with a battle!

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.210
And I’ll catch them!

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.330
Huh?

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.260
Where’d they go?!

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.130
They’re hiding under the soil.
See?

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.960
So they are...

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.060
If you’re going to catch the Digda,
it’s okay to pull up the carrots.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.410
Now’s the perfect time
to harvest them.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.500
All right. Let’s do it!

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.440
Yeah!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.770
Aceburn, help us out!

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.750
Where’d you go, where’d you go?!

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:38.410
This is kinda fun!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.680
Whoa... I’m covered in mud!

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:45.250
Your clothes are always gonna get dirty in the fields.
Don’t worry about it!

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:49.150
Makes sense...
Yeah, I guess they would!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.610
You’re not getting away!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:56.510
Here!

00:08:58.450 --> 00:08:59.810
Satoshi, it’s heading your way!

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:01.840
All right, it’s here!

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:05.900
Dugtrio!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:08.970
All right! Monster Ball, Go!

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.210
Over there!

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.120
Huh? Where?

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:24.660
This way!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:25.460
Where exactly?!

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.960
There’s too many of them...

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.830
I can’t keep track!

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:29.960
There!

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.460
Sorry, Satoshi...

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.220
Go, did you just try
to catch Satoshi?

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:38.240
I caught a Satoshi!

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.260
Of course I wasn’t!

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:53.890
They left...

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:54.770
Yeah...

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.050
We failed...

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.370
That was a great help!

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.370
Thanks to you,
we’ve harvested a lot of carrots!

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:09.770
How about we leave the rest
for tomorrow?

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.500
Sure...

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.420
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:27.810
I get the feeling that Dugtrio
was kinda like their leader.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:32.820
Yeah. If I catch it,
maybe the Digda will stop coming.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.780
I thought of something...

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.050
What is it?

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:41.660
The Dugtrio and the Digda were really coordinated
in running away, weren’t they?

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:47.540
Compared to them, we were all over the place.
Maybe that’s why we didn’t have any luck.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.040
I get it...

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:51.420
Teamwork, huh?

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:56.420
What if we have someone overseeing everything
and giving us commands?

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:59.180
You’d be perfect
for doing that, Koharu!

00:10:59.180 --> 00:10:59.900
Right!

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:01.660
Huh? M-Me?

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.210
It’s all up to you, Koharu.

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:04.750
We’re counting on you.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:13.440
Okay. I’ll give it a try!

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.530
All right!

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.820
Everything’s ready.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:24.950
Hey!

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.450
Okay!

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:31.840
I see... So you’re going to
give them instructions from here.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:32.460
Yeah!

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:38.960
I can watch over the whole field, predict where
the Dugtrio and Digda are going, and tell Go and Satoshi.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:42.760
I set up those flags
thinking some markers would make it easier.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.970
You’ve really
thought this through...

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:49.070
They’re here!

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:50.010
Yeah!

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:52.690
Digda!

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:56.860
It’s headed for the blue flag!

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:58.630
All right.

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:00.240
The blue flag!

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.330
Over there! It’s close!

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.520
Here!

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.410
Leave it to me!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.120
Go!

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:22.470
Digda’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:24.190
I caught a Digda!

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:25.430
Good job, Go!

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.830
Okay, it worked. That’s great!

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.190
There’s still plenty more!

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:34.940
Yeah.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:40.920
Dugtrio!

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:42.070
The leader’s turned up!

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.420
The red flag!
Head for the red flag!

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.690
The fastest one is Dugtrio!
Get ahead of it!

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:07.900
Got it!

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:08.880
There it is.

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:27.990
Now!

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.160
Go!

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:49.800
Dugtrio’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.430
All right!

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:54.050
I caught Dugtrio!

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.810
Great!

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:15.790
Oh, thank you so much,
everyone!

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:19.250
Superb teamwork out there.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.680
Easy!

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:24.070
Now maybe the Digda
will stop coming to the field.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.900
I wonder about that...

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.230
They’ve run off for now, but...

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:32.430
What could’ve caused the Dugtrio and Digda
to suddenly turn up in the field?

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:36.110
They used to live on the hill
across from the farm...

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:38.440
But they never came to
the fields before.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:42.140
Maybe we can figure something out
if we take a look at that hill!

00:14:42.140 --> 00:14:44.280
Yeah. Let’s go!

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.350
Yeah!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.570
This isn’t good, meow.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.200
Fields feel so nice...

00:14:56.200 --> 00:15:00.210
Napping under the sun is the best!

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:07.820
You said you saw the brat boy nearby,
but all you wanna do is nap, meow!

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:13.510
When you see some wide, open place...
You just stop caring about the details...

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:20.140
You all slacking off like that is why we ran out of food,
and I had to resort to growing some, meow!

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:26.610
Hyper Automated Farm Work Machine:
Nyarth Scarecrow #2, you’re up, meow!

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:46.250
I’m giving them lots of water,
but they’re just drooping over, meow.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:50.630
That means we need...
Music, start, meow!

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:00.140
Listening to music makes plants
grow better, meow!

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.230
What’s this noise?!
It’s so loud!

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:07.610
If this was happening,
I’m not surprised the Digda would run away from it!

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.490
What’s going on here?!

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:15.240
If you say “What’s going on here?!”...

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:18.330
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:22.340
To protect the world from devastation.

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:25.170
To preserve world peace.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.420
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:31.380
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:32.620
Musashi!

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:33.840
Kojiro!

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:37.700
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.680
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.990
Just kidding, meow!

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:49.530
So you’ve come, brat boys!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.220
Huh? What was that?

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:52.530
I can’t hear a thing!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:56.580
Darn it, meow!
Music, stop, meow!

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:07.300
So <i>you</i> drove the Digda
out of their home!

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:09.420
Give it back to them,
right now!

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:13.520
Hah! You’ve got some nerve,
cutting into our relaxation time!

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:16.180
Well, I was getting
sorta bored of the fields...

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:20.490
Stealing suits us more than
sleeping in fields anyway!

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:23.800
We’ll be taking that Pikachu!

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.270
Vending, come on!

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:38.780
Rocket...

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.000
Vending...

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.910
Secret!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:42.790
Clatter clatter!

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.880
What’re we gonna get?!

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.870
The Mole Pokémon, Mogurew!

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:03.570
The Mouse Pokémon, Sandpan!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.350
Then I’ll use this one!

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:11.290
Dugtrio! Dig!

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.110
Mogurew! Drill Liner!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:20.120
You use Drill Liner, too,
Sandpan!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.040
Bulldoze!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.300
Huh? What’s going on?
I can’t tell! I can’t tell!

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:39.300
A battle of epic proportions
must be unfolding, meow!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.800
Are you sure?

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.270
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:56.650
All right, now! Sand Hell!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.320
Wh-Wh-What?

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.690
We couldn’t be...

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:14.460
What an awful feeling!

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.020
The soil’s really soft.

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:35.260
It’s a great color...

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:38.150
<i>Thanks for the food!</i>

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.670
Go on, eat as much as you want!

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:44.630
I made loads of dishes
with the carrots you picked!

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:46.440
This curry’s full of carrots!

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:48.200
The cake looks tasty, too!

00:19:48.610 --> 00:19:49.610
I’ll have seconds!

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:50.400
Sure.

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:01.300
Those’re the guys
that were with Dugtrio.

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:11.090
I get it. The Digda will have a hard time
without their leader.

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:17.680
Here.
I’m leaving Dugtrio with you.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:20.040
Are you sure?

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:20.900
Yeah.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.160
I have this one already.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:27.170
And I learned something
when looking through some information.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:34.170
If a Dugtrio digs through a field,
it leaves the soil perfectly tilled and ideal for planting crops!

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:37.650
In some regions,
they are used on farms!

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:43.680
So I think it’ll make a good partner
for you, Mr. Endo.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:48.580
I see... I couldn’t ask for
better help with the fields!

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:53.060
I’ll be growing even tastier vegetables than before,
so would you help me with that?

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.460
I’m counting on you!

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:22.500
What?

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:23.420
Koharu?

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:26.160
Wide, open spaces
just make you want to run, right?

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:27.670
Yeah!

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:28.720
You really...?

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.390
Wait for us!

